# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Game data must NEVER be committed. The port reads the user's own disc at
# runtime; this repository contains code only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ref/
*.bin
*.cue
*.iso
*.img
*.ccd
*.sub
*.mds
*.mdf
*.chd
*.pbp
*.DAT
*.dat
*.XAI
*.STX
*.ALL
SLES_*
SLUS_*
SLPS_*
SLPM_*
SCES_*
SYSTEM.CNF

# Build output. The pattern must stay ANCHORED: an unanchored "build*/" also
# matches src/build/, the release-identification layer, and silently kept every
# file in it out of the repository. It still covers the third-party checkout
# that -DQ2PSX_FETCH_SDL3=ON drops under the build tree, because that tree is
# itself a top-level build directory.
/build*/
out/
cmake-build-*/
_deps/
*.o
*.obj
*.exe
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.lib
*.a
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
compile_commands.json
.cache/

# Release staging. scripts/package.py assembles archives here; they are build
# output, not sources, and they are attached to a GitHub release instead.
/dist/

# Ready-to-launch local client, runtime files and the user's disc/configuration.
/.install/

# Original commercial branding and promotional reference material.
/.branding/originals/
# Local illustrated design references contain original commercial artwork.
/.branding/design/
# Local reconstructed typefaces and specimens derived from retail references.
/.branding/fonts/

# Agent build logs, captures and temporary test profiles.
/.agents/tmp/

# Python bytecode, from the release tooling in scripts/ and tools/.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editors
.vs/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/launch.json
.idea/
*.user
*.swp
*~

# Extracted / working data. .tmp/ is where `q2psx-inspect export` writes, and
# what it writes is decoded game data — the same rule as the block above.
extracted/
dump/
.tmp/
*.log
/artifacts

# Rendered frames. `q2psx-inspect render` and the client's --shot write these,
# and what they draw is the disc's own artwork, so they fall under the very
# first rule in this file. Seven had been committed to the repository root --
# a title screen, a HUD test, two model renders, two level renders and an
# accidental screenshot of a terminal window -- while the README said the
# repository contains no game assets. scripts/check_paths.py now fails CI on
# any that come back.
*.ppm
*.pgm
*.pnm
/*.png
/*.bmp
/*.tga
